  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Reproductive Health Supplies Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To meet the contraceptive needs of over 20 million women per year; to reduce unintended pregnancies and maternal deaths; to improve maternal, newborn and child health, and to contribute to universal health coverage. This will be achieved by funding activities to improve the availability, quality, supply and access to key reproductive health commodities, including for those in hard to reach areas. This will support women&apos;s rights and the 2030 agenda.</narrative>
  </description>
